prompts.body:
Capture EVERY animation in the Curate iOS app, exactly as it runs today, as footage clips in the curate-motion library. The founder wants the ads to use the app's exact animations, not re-creations. Curate is a fashion stylist app whose mascot is Zee, a black plush kitten; 1.5.0 build 262 is the App Store build.

**Sources**
- **App code:** /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/.worktrees/app-emma-262 (release/1.5.0-262 @5aff9592, already built for the simulator). Read-only; no app code changes. You may add probe files in a worktree of your own if needed.
- **Emma's account is live** on simulator "Emma Marketing 17PM", UDID B0202502-C8FB-4DAA-8E29-EAE4866B0C14 (booted, signed in, 49 wardrobe pieces, 73 photos in the roll).
  - ALWAYS target this exact UDID, never `booted`: other sessions hijacked a recording once.
  - Never touch the "iPhone 17" simulator or any other session's simulator.
  - Her password is in SSM /curate/marketing/emma-password, if you ever need to sign in again. Never print it.
- **Library repo:** /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/curate-motion. Read AGENTS.md first and follow it: the naming grammar, `tools/catalog add --kind footage …`, `tools/capture.sh`, licences/status, and `tools/sync push`.
- **Existing footage** in /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/footage/emma/: photo-scan-v1.mov (a clean 6-minute hero take of the whole scan), onboarding-v1.mov (clean), signup-v1.mov (messy). Cut clips from these where they already show a moment cleanly, instead of re-recording.

**Steps**
1. **Inventory.** List every animation and motion moment in the app from the code (file:line), grouped by screen. At least:
   - the front door type reel ("Try it. Style it. Wear it.");
   - onboarding steps;
   - the privacy shield with Zee peeking;
   - the selfie step (Zee over the ring) and camera (ring opens, hints, shutter, "That's you!", hand-back);
   - Photos-off "Two taps" with the Yay;
   - the scan roll (real speed, Zee's magnifier, photos lifting into Picked);
   - the "Up big" pieces wait (Zee's lines, piece names, first piece lifting out);
   - "Tell me when it's ready" with the notification ask;
   - the Curate-at-work pill → "Your wardrobe is ready ›" → Zee's cheer screen;
   - the Wardrobe tab with pure-float pieces;
   - Zee asks on an empty wardrobe;
   - Zee's 13 extra moments (ob83);
   - the chat: the Mist look, the composer, Zee's thinking lines while a look is made, the look card landing, question cards, the location ask (the foggy window), Adjust, Style notes (notebook, close-ups floating), the chat drawer sliding in;
   - Try-ons (avatar, Add an item sheet, the result);
   - the in-app update sheet;
   - haptic-free transitions between tabs;
   - any loading shimmer that's on brand.

   Write the inventory to curate-motion/library/footage/INVENTORY.md, with a status column.
2. **Capture each one** on Emma's simulator, from her REAL account wherever the state can be reached:
   - Use `xcrun simctl io <UDID> recordVideo --codec=hevc` for quality, with a clean status bar (9:41, full battery, full signal).
   - Real speed. Take 2+ clean takes of the important ones. Mist look; check that it's on for her.
   - Navigate with what works on the simulator (simctl, idb or AppleScript taps if available; check what earlier agents used).
   - Where a state can't be reached on her account or on a simulator (the selfie CAMERA, since the simulator has no camera; maybe the pieces wait if no import is running; error states), use the app's own dev probes in lib/dev/ with Emma's REAL assets as inputs. For the camera, use her selfie at curate-motion/library/people/emma/ as the stand-in feed. Label those clips `source: probe` in the manifest.
   - Never show old screens (e.g. the old "Your wardrobe is already in your photos" door), stale assets or other people's data.
3. **Trim** each moment into its own clip: lossless, or high-quality HEVC/H.264, cut at the start and end of the animation with about 0.5 s of handle each side. Also keep the full takes. Name and register each clip with `tools/catalog add` as kind footage, with:
   - tags `moment=<slug>`, `screen=<screen>`, `appBuild=262`, `persona=emma`, `source=app|probe`;
   - status draft;
   - the licence preset for our own footage, per AGENTS.md.
   Example id grammar: `footage.emma.scan-roll.v1`.
4. **Paid actions:** server spend cap **$2 total**. Chat looks cost about $0.19 each, try-ons a few cents. Use at most about 5 chat looks and 2 try-ons. Reuse looks that are already in her chat where possible. Log the spend.
5. **Push:** `tools/catalog build && tools/catalog validate`, then `tools/sync push`.
   - Check that the earlier sync bug fix is in tools/lib/s3sync.ts (EMPTY_BODY). The main session may still be pushing; wait until `ps aux | grep "tools/sync push"` shows none before you push.
   - Don't git commit or push; the main session will.
6. **Live tracker.** Write /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/tracker/captures.js as `window.CURATE_CAPTURES = {updated, phase, done, total, sections:[{title, items:[{path,label}]}], log:[{t,text}]}`, atomically, after each captured moment.
   - Paths are relative to the tracker. Make small mp4 or jpg previews in marketing/videos/footage/_previews/.
   - The main session will wire the page.
7. **Phone view.** At the end, publish an artifact (load the artifact-design skill first; icon "video") with the inventory and small preview clips of every moment, under 64 MB. Give the URL.
8. **Leave Emma's simulator** booted and signed in, on the Wardrobe tab.

**Rules:** no app code changes, no prod changes beyond Emma's own usage, never print secrets, use they/them for the founder.

**Report:** the inventory counts (total / captured / via probe / not possible), the clip ids, the spend, any blockers, and the artifact URL.

Capture SCREENSHOTS of every screen and state of the Curate iOS app (1.5.0, build 262) from the marketing persona Emma's real account, and add them to the curate-motion library. Curate is a fashion stylist app whose mascot is Zee, a black plush kitten. The screenshots are for ads, App Store pages, the website and social posts.

**Setup (read first)**
- Repo: /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/curate-motion. Read AGENTS.md, RULES.md and library/brand/BRAND.md, and follow them: id grammar, `tools/catalog add`, licences, approvals, sync.
- library/footage/INVENTORY.md lists every screen and animation, with file:line. Use it as your checklist.
- **Emma's simulator:** "Emma Marketing 17PM", UDID B0202502-C8FB-4DAA-8E29-EAE4866B0C14 (booted, signed in, 49 wardrobe pieces, Mist look, location Astoria).
  - ALWAYS target that exact UDID, never `booted`.
  - Never touch the "iPhone 17" simulator or other sessions' simulators.
  - Her password is in SSM /curate/marketing/emma-password, if needed. Never print it.
- The previous capture agent's scripts are in curate-motion/tools/capture/ (s.sh, pr.sh, ui.py and others, for driving and recording the simulator). Reuse them.
- For states the real account can't reach (the selfie camera, Photos-off, Zee's 13 moments, the update sheet), that agent used dev probes on a separate simulator, "Emma Probe 17PM" (CE85B987, now shut down), from the worktree /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/.worktrees/app-capture-262, with Emma's real assets swapped in. Do the same, and tag those shots `source:probe`.

**What to capture**
1. **Every screen and meaningful state.** That includes:
   - the front door;
   - each onboarding step;
   - the privacy shield;
   - the selfie step and camera hints;
   - Photos-off "Two taps";
   - the scan roll mid-scan;
   - the Up big wait;
   - pieces arriving;
   - "Your wardrobe is ready" with the cheer;
   - the import review;
   - the Wardrobe tab (top, scrolled, each filter chip);
   - piece detail and edit;
   - Add item;
   - the duplicate review;
   - the empty chat with Zee;
   - Zee thinking;
   - each look card;
   - multiple looks;
   - question cards;
   - the location ask;
   - Adjust;
   - the Style notes notebook;
   - the chat drawer;
   - the Try-ons tab and a result;
   - Profile and Settings;
   - the "Curate at work" pill.
2. **Format:** full-resolution PNGs at the device's native 1320×2868, with a clean status bar (`xcrun simctl status_bar override`: 9:41, full battery and signal, no carrier).
   - For the most important 20–25 hero screens, make 2 variants each: the plain screenshot, and an App Store-ready 1290×2796 (6.7") PNG.
   - Check ASC's accepted sizes. 1320×2868 is the 6.9" set and is also accepted.
3. **Quality checks.** Look at EVERY shot. Never ship one with:
   - another session's app or banner;
   - a red error, a debug banner or an overflow stripe;
   - old screens (e.g. the old "Your wardrobe is already in your photos" door);
   - another person's data;
   - prices or shopping.
   Retake it instead.
4. **Register** each shot with `tools/catalog add --kind screenshot` if that kind exists. Otherwise add a `screenshot` kind to the schema (schemas/asset.ts plus KIND_FIELDS) in a small, clean commit-ready change, and document it in AGENTS.md's kind list.
   - Ids look like `screenshot.emma.wardrobe-top.v1`.
   - Tags: screen, state, appBuild=262, persona=emma, source=app|probe, size.
   - Licence `curate`, status draft.
   - Then `tools/catalog build && tools/catalog validate && tools/sync push`.
5. **Server spend cap: $1.** Only spend if a new chat look or try-on is truly needed; reuse her existing chat looks and try-ons.
6. **Phone view.** Publish a single-file artifact (load the artifact-design skill first; icon "image"), with images inlined as small JPEG thumbnails and the file under 15 MB, grouped by screen. Give the URL.
7. **Live progress.** Write /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/tracker/screens.js as `window.CURATE_SCREENS = {updated, phase, done, total, sections:[{title, items:[{path,label}]}], log:[{t,text}]}`, atomically. Paths are relative to the tracker; put thumbnails in marketing/videos/footage/_screens/.

**Rules**
- No app code changes, except probe stand-in assets in your own worktree.
- No git commits in curate-motion; the main session commits.
- Never print secrets.
- Use they/them for the founder.
- Leave Emma's simulator booted and signed in on the Wardrobe tab, and shut down any probe simulator you start.

**Report:** the counts (total, real, probe), the ids, the hero list, the spend, the artifact URL, and any schema change you made.

Explore MORE marketing video concepts for Curate, a fashion stylist iOS app (US App Store) whose mascot is Zee, a black plush kitten. Also prepare a full app EXPLAINER video concept. The founder asked: "explore more concepts, like some really cool transitions… these go on TikTok and Insta. Also 10 s is a bit short, we need all spectrum, short to lengthy, and also a proper video to explain our entire app."

**What already exists (build on it; don't redo it):**
- The Remotion project at /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/remotion: remotion 4.0.535 and react 19.2.3, rendering with the installed Google Chrome (see remotion.config.ts). Zee frames are in remotion/public/zee/ (from the zee-sharp-v1 pack), and there's tools/capture.sh.
- 5 concepts with 10–12 s motion tests in marketing/videos/cuts/ (c1–c5 v1/v2):
  - c1 "Already in your photos";
  - c2 "Meet Zee";
  - c3 "What do I wear today?";
  - c4 "Two taps to a closet";
  - c5 "See it on you".
  Read their storyboards in tracker/status.js.
- 8 Mixkit tracks in marketing/videos/music/ (licences in music/licences.json: commercial and ads OK; no broadcast and no Content ID), plus 2 Pixabay links.
- **The live tracker the founder watches:** marketing/videos/tracker/index.html, which re-reads status.js and assets.js every 3 s.
  - You now OWN status.js; the earlier video agent is finished. Keep c1–c5 as they are, and ADD your new concepts as c6, c7, … plus an "explainer" entry, using the same concept shape (id, title, idea, status, progress, steps, files, plus the hook, words, storyboard, music and channels fields the earlier agent added; read index.html to see what it renders).
  - Rewrite status.js atomically (temp file + mv) after EVERY step, and append plain-English log lines.
  - Do NOT touch assets.js; the assets agent owns it.
- **Assets in progress:** a marketing persona "Emma" (27, NYC, olive skin, long dark-brown hair; face reference assets/persona/emma-face-B-v1.jpg), her ~50-piece wardrobe and her camera roll are being generated by another agent in marketing/videos/assets/. Real app footage is NOT recorded yet; it will be recorded from Emma's account later.

**What to make**
1. **New concepts: 6–8 for TikTok, Reels and Shorts,** built around really cool TRANSITIONS and trends. Ideas to explore:
   - match cuts (a phone-photo outfit morphing into the app's floating piece);
   - a whip-pan or swipe between looks;
   - "outfit check" snap transitions;
   - masking through Zee or through the phone frame;
   - 3D phone flips;
   - kinetic-type wipes;
   - a closet-door reveal;
   - a hand-tap-to-transition;
   - "POV: you never know what to wear";
   - a "get ready with me" format;
   - a before/after closet chaos to calm;
   - a day of outfits (Mon–Sun) in one continuous move;
   - a weather-swap transition (rain to sun swaps the look).
   Each one is native-feeling for TikTok and Insta, with a hook in the first 1 s.
2. **The full length spectrum.** For the concepts, cover:
   - **6 s** bumpers;
   - **15 s**;
   - **30 s**;
   - **60 s**;
   - **90 s–2 min** stories.
   Mark which length each concept is made for, and show how the strongest concepts scale (a 6/15/30 cut-down plan).
3. **THE APP EXPLAINER, 2–3 min.** A proper video that explains the whole app, for the website, YouTube and onboarding. Script it scene by scene with a time code:
   - the problem;
   - meet Zee;
   - your wardrobe from your photos (the privacy shield, selfie, scan, pieces arriving);
   - pure-float pieces;
   - chat with Zee (asking for an outfit, Zee's thinking, question cards, Adjust, Style notes);
   - weather and location;
   - Try-ons;
   - "Tell me when it's ready";
   - the outro call to action.
   Write a voiceover script (warm and simple; American English), on-screen words (few), the music plan, and the footage needed per scene (from Emma's account).
   - **Voiceover:** note the options (record a human; or TTS, which would cost money and needs the founder's OK, so don't generate it), and DON'T make any paid voice.
4. **Motion tests.** For the 3 most promising new transition concepts, plus the explainer's opening 20–30 s, render tests in 1080×1920 (the explainer also in 1920×1080), 30 fps, H.264, small files.
   - Use ONLY Zee's frames, Geist type, abstract shapes, and the founder-approved GENERATED assets once they exist in marketing/videos/assets/ (garment product shots and Emma's photos are fine to use when present).
   - NO app footage, no probe or test data, no old screens.
   - Put them in cuts/ as c6-motion-test-v1.mp4, explainer-open-v1.mp4 etc., and add them to the tracker as each one renders.
5. **Phone view.** The founder is often on their phone, and the local tracker only opens on their Mac. When you're done, publish ONE artifact (load the artifact-design skill first; icon "video") that shows all concepts c1–c(n) and the explainer: storyboards, scripts, lengths, and the motion-test videos embedded via the Artifact tool's `files` (keep the total under 64 MB per publish, downscaling copies if needed). Give the URL in your report.

**Rules**
- Read memory in /Users/saikumar/.claude/projects/-Users-saikumar-Desktop-Curate-curate-app/memory/: marketing-videos.md, curate-brand-guidelines.md, never-show-the-pipeline.md, shop-tab-preview.md (no shopping or prices), keep-every-version.md, ask-before-spending-api-credits.md, seed-population-program.md (the FTC note: no fake testimonials).
- No paid calls; it all renders locally.
- No prod, no simulators of other sessions.
- Never print secrets. Use they/them for the founder.

**Report:** the concepts list (one line each, length and channel), the explainer outline, the motion-test files, the artifact URL, and your top 3 picks.

Design the architecture for, and scaffold, **curate-motion**: Curate's dedicated project for motion-graphics marketing videos. Curate is a fashion stylist iOS app whose mascot is Zee, a black plush kitten. The founder wants everything (accounts, animations, images, footage, music) in ONE place, made once and reused, so every new ad is ASSEMBLED from the library instead of regenerated.

**Approved:**
- code and lists (manifests) live on GitHub as a PRIVATE repo;
- big media (video, images, audio) lives in a PRIVATE Amazon S3 bucket, with a one-command sync.

**What exists today** (in /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/; read it, don't move it yet; two other agents are still writing there):
- **remotion/:** a Remotion 4.0.535 project (react 19.2.3; renders with the installed Google Chrome via remotion.config.ts; Zee frames in public/zee/; garments in public/garments; tools/capture.sh; compositions for concepts c1–c5+).
- **cuts/:** motion tests.
- **music/:** 8 Mixkit tracks plus licences.json.
- **assets/:** "Emma", the marketing persona (27, NYC, olive skin; face reference persona/emma-face-B-v1.jpg; persona.md), with garments/ (about 50 AI product shots + manifest.json), roll/ (her camera roll), selfie/, tryon/, stock/ (Pexels/Unsplash with licences) and _thumbs/.
- **references/:** a breakdown of a creator reel.
- **tracker/:** index.html is a live local page re-reading status.js, assets.js and references.js every 3 s.
- Zee's source pack: /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/research/zee-pack/app/zee-sharp-v1/.
- App code (for brand tokens and fonts): /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/curate-app (lib/core/theme, lib/features/look/).

**Deliverables**
1. **ARCHITECTURE.md** in the new repo, plus a phone-viewable Artifact of it (load the artifact-design skill first; icon "diagram"; use a simple diagram). It covers:
   - **The folder layout:**
     - `library/`: brand, zee, people/<persona>, wardrobe/<persona>, camera-roll/<persona>, footage/<moment>, music, references;
     - `motion/`: reusable Remotion components;
     - `ads/`: each ad is a composition built from library refs + motion components + a track;
     - `renders/`: by ad/channel/length;
     - `tools/`;
     - RULES.md.
   - **The asset catalog:** one typed manifest schema (JSON Schema or zod) per asset kind. Give each asset a stable id, path in S3, sha256, dimensions/duration, tags (persona, garment category/colour, moment, mood, BPM/beat map for music), source and LICENCE (required), cost, and created-by. Assets are referenced by id in ads, never by raw path.
   - **The S3 layer:**
     - bucket naming;
     - a private bucket with Block Public Access, SSE, versioning and lifecycle rules;
     - `tools/sync` (pull/push by manifest, content-addressed or path plus sha check);
     - how local `library/` maps to S3;
     - .gitignore for media.
     Weigh Git LFS vs S3 briefly and say why S3.
   - **The Remotion structure:** a `motion/` component library. Start the list from what exists:
     - PhoneFrame, ZeeActor, KineticType, BeatClock (BPM → frames);
     - PopOut (scale-from-source with overshoot and return), TitleBehind, FlashPrint, ScanTrace, Ellipse, StrokeFrame, WhipPan, ClosetReveal;
     - plus format presets (9:16 1080×1920, 4:5, 1:1, 16:9, App Store preview sizes) and length variants (6/15/30/60/90–120 s);
     - `ads/<ad-id>/` with props validated by zod, so one ad renders to many formats and lengths.
   - **Personas and accounts:** how a marketing persona's app account is recorded (email, NOT the password). Secrets go in AWS SSM or GCP Secret Manager, never in git. Also how footage captured from that account is catalogued by moment and app build.
   - **Footage capture:** the tools/capture flow (simulator recording, clean status bar), naming, and the manifest entry.
   - **Rules:**
     - licences are tracked and required;
     - no shopping or prices;
     - never show the pipeline;
     - no logos;
     - FTC (personas never vouch for products);
     - an "AI-generated" note where platforms require it;
     - the Remotion licence (free for teams of ≤3, else paid).
   - **The tracker → library browser:** the local page turns into a browser of the catalog plus a render queue and status.
   - **Migration plan** from marketing/videos/ into the repo, as exact steps, run LATER by the main session once the other agents finish.
2. **Scaffold** the repo at /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/curate-motion:
   - `git init`, README, ARCHITECTURE.md, RULES.md, the schemas, tools/sync (a script using the aws cli), .gitignore, and a minimal motion/ folder.
   - Either a copy of the existing Remotion project structure re-laid-out (copy the code, not media), or a fresh Remotion 4.0.535 workspace that compiles (`npx tsc --noEmit` or `npx remotion compositions` works).
   - Commit messages end with: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
3. **Create the private GitHub repo** with `gh repo create saicurate/curate-motion --private` (check that the saicurate org is where the other Curate repos live: `gh repo list saicurate --limit 5`) and push. Verify it's PRIVATE.
4. **Create the S3 bucket** in us-east-1 (e.g. `curate-motion-library-<account-id>`):
   - block all public access, default encryption, versioning on, and a lifecycle rule to expire non-current versions after 90 days;
   - tag it project=curate-motion;
   - verify with get-public-access-block.
   - Don't upload media yet; that's the migration.

**Rules**
- Don't move or delete anything in marketing/videos/.
- Never print secrets.
- No paid model calls.
- Use they/them for the founder.

**Report:** the repo URL (and that it's private), the bucket name and its settings, the artifact URL, the component list, and the migration steps.

Build the ASSETS for Curate's marketing videos. Curate is a fashion stylist iOS app whose mascot is Zee, a black plush kitten; 1.5.0 is live in the US App Store. The ads target AMERICANS.

**The founder approved:**
- one woman persona, "Emma", 27, New York;
- her style as a mix: NYC minimal for the week, casual for the weekend, and one dressy going-out look;
- AI image spend of up to **$20 total (a hard cap)**.

**LIVE TRACKER: the founder watches every step.** Write /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/tracker/assets.js (atomically: temp file + mv) after EVERY meaningful step, in this shape: `window.CURATE_ASSETS = { updated, phase, spend (USD so far), cap: 20, sections:[{title, note, items:[{path,label}]}], log:[{t,text}] }`.
- Paths are RELATIVE to the tracker folder, e.g. "../assets/garments/white-tee.jpg". Make small JPEG thumbnails (about 400 px) for the tracker in assets/_thumbs/, and keep the full-size files.
- Log lines are plain English, short, with no file paths and no jargon. Use ISO times.
- Do NOT touch status.js; another agent owns it.

**Assets folder:** /Users/saikumar/Desktop/Curate/marketing/videos/assets/{garments,persona,roll,selfie,tryon,stock,_thumbs}. Keep every version (memory keep-every-version.md); never overwrite a picked image.

**Before you start, READ** in /Users/saikumar/.claude/projects/-Users-saikumar-Desktop-Curate-curate-app/memory/:
- ask-before-spending-api-credits.md (the $20 is approved; track every call's cost, and stop and report if you'd exceed it);
- track-everything-in-benches.md;
- tryon-engine-bakeoff.md (which image models work well and their prices, e.g. Nano Banana / Gemini image);
- shop-tab-preview.md (no prices or shopping);
- curate-brand-guidelines.md;
- seed-population-program.md (the FTC note: personas never vouch for merchandise);
- identify-seed-users.md;
- email-otp verification notes (curate-email-otp-verification.md: the test123.com OTP bypass);
- platform-secrets-shared.md;
- wardrobe-extraction-pipeline.md;
- wardrobe-item-edit-endpoint.md.

Key: the Gemini API key is in AWS SSM /curate/gemini-api-key (us-east-1) or GCP secret gemini-api-key. Never print it. NEVER use the GCP secret anthropic-api-key or any Anthropic image use.

**Steps, in order, updating the tracker at each one:**

1. **Emma's face: get the founder's pick first.**
   - Write a short persona sheet: age 27, New York, her job (e.g. junior designer), and a concrete look (hair, skin tone, build, height). Make her believable and relatable for a broad American audience.
   - Generate **3 candidate portraits**: natural, photoreal, phone-camera quality, not model-glossy.
   - Put them in a tracker section "Emma: pick her face (A / B / C)". Log "Waiting for the founder to pick Emma's face", then CONTINUE with step 2 while waiting.
   - Message the main session (SendMessage to "main") when the candidates are up.
   - Only generate face-dependent images after you get a pick message.
2. **Her wardrobe: about 50 pieces.**
   - Product photos on a clean light seamless background, 3:4, consistent soft studio light, the whole garment visible, NO brand logos or text on any garment.
   - The real American mix:
     - denim: straight-leg jeans in light and dark wash, a denim jacket;
     - basics: white tee, black tee, grey crewneck sweatshirt, hoodie;
     - shirts: a flannel and an oxford;
     - knits: a cardigan and a cable-knit sweater;
     - for work: a blazer, trousers, a midi skirt;
     - outerwear: a trench, a puffer, a wool coat, a varsity jacket;
     - dresses: a little black dress and a slip dress;
     - activewear: leggings and a sports bra/tank set;
     - shoes: white leather sneakers, retro runners, loafers, ankle boots, cowboy boots, heels, sandals;
     - bags: a tote, a crossbody, a mini bag;
     - accessories: a baseball cap, a beanie, a scarf, sunglasses, a belt, gold hoops.
   - Generate them in batches of about 10, and post each batch to the tracker as it lands ("Wardrobe: 10 of 50").
   - Check each image. Redo any with logos, extra items, a cut-off garment, or AI artefacts.
   - Keep a manifest: assets/garments/manifest.json with name, category, colour, file and cost.
3. **After the face pick: her camera roll, about 30 photos.**
   - Emma (the picked face, as a reference image) wearing pieces from HER wardrobe (pass the garment images as references) in everyday American places: a NYC coffee shop, a subway platform, a Brooklyn street, a park, an office, a farmers market, a rooftop at golden hour, a beach day, a mirror selfie in her apartment, a night out.
   - Mostly casual phone-photo framing, some full-body and some half.
   - Each photo should show 2–4 identifiable wardrobe pieces; record which in roll/manifest.json.
   - Also make her **selfie** (head and shoulders, good light), for the selfie scene, and **2 try-on base photos** (full body, plain outfit, neutral background, front-facing), for the Try-ons tab.
